NAME
     passwd - change a password

SYNOPSIS
     passwd [-l|-u|-d|-S] [USER]

DESCRIPTION
     passwd changes a user's password, asking for the old one first
     unless root is asking. The hashes are PBKDF2-SHA256 in
     /etc/shadow, which only root can read.

OPTIONS
     -l   lock the account
     -u   unlock it
     -d   remove the password entirely
     -S   say what state the account is in

SEE ALSO
     login(1), su(1), useradd(8)
